# Hover and Click Anywhere

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Events between points and on unhover

Set `layout.hoveranywhere` and `layout.clickanywhere` to receive events even
when no point is hit. These remain `plotly_hover` and `plotly_click` events:
`points` is empty between points, while `xvals`/`yvals` contain axis values and
top-level `xPixel`/`yPixel` contain cursor pixels. Point pixel fields describe
point centres when a point is present. `plotly_unhover` is forwarded too.

Move between markers, click empty plot space, then leave a marker or the plot.
The output shows the latest event without assuming a nonempty points list.

````elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}
alias Plotly.Kino.PlotlyLive

output = Kino.Frame.new()

chart =
  Figure.new()
  |> Figure.add_trace(Scatter.new(x: [1, 3, 5], y: [1, 4, 2], mode: "markers"))
  |> Figure.update_layout(
    title: "Hover or click anywhere in the axes",
    hoveranywhere: true, clickanywhere: true,
    xaxis: %{range: [0, 6]}, yaxis: %{range: [0, 5]}
  )
  |> PlotlyLive.new()

listener = spawn(fn ->
  for _ <- 1..1000 do
    receive do
      {:anywhere_event, %{"type" => type, "data" => data}} ->
        details = Map.take(data, ["points", "xvals", "yvals", "xPixel", "yPixel"])
        text = "**#{type}**\n\n```elixir\n#{inspect(details, pretty: true)}\n```"
        Kino.Frame.render(output, Kino.Markdown.new(text))
    after
      60_000 -> :timeout
    end
  end
end)

for filter <- [:hover, :click, :unhover] do
  PlotlyLive.subscribe(chart, listener, :anywhere_event, filter)
end

Kino.Layout.grid([chart, output])
````
